WEBVTT

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.630
Serizawa-san, it’s me, Kondou.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:08.420
Enter!

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:10.290
I’m coming in.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.080
I believe you called for us.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:24.300
Yeah.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:29.380
You see, we have a great
idea for how to remedy

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:31.210
the Roshigumi’s need for more men.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.220
My! What do you have in mind?

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:39.030
The Shogunate sent this

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:41.100
practitioner of Western medicine to us.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:43.310
He is Kodo Yukimura-dono.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:45.600
The Shogunate sent him?

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:46.820
Indeed.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.480
Under the Shogunate’s orders,

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:52.070
Yukimura-dono and I began advancing

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.980
the preparations some time back.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.620
When exactly was “some time back”?

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.120
It was some time ago.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.880
So what is this excellent idea?

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:13.810
Ow!

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:15.330
That’s enough, cur.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:17.010
Remove yourself.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.180
Fine!

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:56.360
They’re taking forever...

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:58.310
Whatcha think Kondou-san and

00:02:58.310 --> 00:02:59.990
the others are talkin’ about?

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:01.910
Orders from the Shogunate, eh?

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:03.490
This smells fishy!

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:06.020
We have Isami-san and Toshi-san.

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:08.370
I doubt things will turn out poorly.

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:11.460
We should leave this in their hands.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.880
Ibuki-kun, shouldn’t you be

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:16.130
massaging Serizawa-san’s shoulders?

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:20.550
He told me to stay here
until they finish talking!

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:42.150
Howling from the Darkness

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:44.510
What was with that scream?

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.160
Somethin’ serious is goin’ down!

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.000
Huh?

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:50.660
What’s wrong?

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:52.410
It won’t open!

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:55.670
Damn, what happened to him?!

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:58.210
Toshi! Sannan-kun!
Don’t let him get out!

00:03:58.210 --> 00:03:59.050
Right!

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:00.170
Move it, Heisuke!

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:03.880
Gen-san, look after things here.

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:04.550
Yeah!

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:06.930
Sano, secure the front.

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:07.430
Got it!

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:09.370
Ibuki-kun!

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:12.520
You’ll only get in our
way if you tag along.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.310
Wh-what was that?!

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.070
Wh-what is he?!

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.710
Humans don’t move like that.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:47.700
Look out, Souji!

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:06.860
If you lack the resolve to kill someone

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:09.320
when you draw that, get out of here!

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:11.990
Shinpachi!

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:18.380
Be careful, Sano!

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:20.380
There’s something weird about him!

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:33.770
Sano-san!

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:41.270
His injury--!

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:48.860
Run for it, Ryunosuke!

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:04.920
Hijikata-san, get away from him! He can--

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:06.300
It’s okay.

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:08.960
Supposedly you can kill it by

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:11.110
piercing its heart or by beheading it.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:17.390
Is everyone uninjured?

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:18.440
Kondou-san!

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:19.630
Are you are all right?

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:25.190
Dang, what the heck was that?

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:35.790
If you lack any real resolve,

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:37.790
don’t waltz out onto a battlefield.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:53.100
I’ve seen that face somewhere before.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.180
Saito, Harada!

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:58.850
Sorry, but I need you
to carry him inside.

00:06:58.850 --> 00:06:59.890
’Kay.

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:01.030
Very well.

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:04.170
Everyone, please gather in the hall.

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:05.230
We need to talk.

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:08.150
That includes you, Ibuki.

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:08.740
Huh?

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:11.210
You saw him.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:23.330
The Bakufu obtained this
through foreign trade.

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:25.500
This medicine is called
the “Water of Life.”

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:30.510
If you drink this, your abilities in
battle will substantially increase.

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:34.510
At the same time, you will obtain
remarkable healing abilities.

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:37.480
But on the other hand, you will lose

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:40.020
the power of thought and your sanity.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:44.640
Meaning that it isn’t full
of nothing but perks, eh?

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:47.790
Indeed. To top it off,
they can only exercise

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:49.280
those powers in the dark.

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:54.690
We call those who drink the medicine

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:57.060
and exhibit these powers “furies.”

00:07:57.530 --> 00:07:58.980
The way he looked...

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:00.830
He was definitely a fury.

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:04.540
I remember! That was Iesato!

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:05.660
That’s right.

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:07.670
Iesato...?

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:11.800
Wasn’t he one of the
guys who left Edo with us?

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:16.050
You used one of our pals to test
out some crazy medicine?!

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:20.200
He was supposed to slice open

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:22.700
his gut for breaking the code.

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:24.600
It’s the same punishment.

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:25.940
That’s no excuse!

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:29.440
He didn’t get to die by seppuku!

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:31.150
That is the only difference.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:36.950
Serizawa-san, I am against
experimenting with this medicine.

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:41.900
When Iesato became a fury,
he didn’t recognize us at all!

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:44.580
I am of like mind.

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:47.920
But according to Yukimura-dono,

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:50.710
there is still plenty
of room for improvement.

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:52.350
And to test it out,

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:55.220
you’d have to experiment
on another person again!

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:57.340
The Shogunate ordered us to do this!

00:08:57.390 --> 00:09:00.430
There is no need to obey
an unreasonable order.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:03.630
Generally, warriors consider

00:09:03.630 --> 00:09:07.860
obeying orders from the
Shogun to be virtuous,

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:11.920
even if they are unreasonable orders.

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:14.990
Serizawa-san, you...!

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:18.900
Although I don’t expect one not born

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:21.650
into a warrior family to understand.

00:09:21.650 --> 00:09:22.830
What was that?!

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:23.750
Toshi!

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:26.980
Considering our current standing,

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:30.130
we cannot ignore the will of the Shogunate.

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:31.560
Sannan-san...!

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:37.840
However, if there is still
room for improvement,

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:42.050
I feel it would be wise for Niimi-san to

00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:45.280
step down from his position as chief

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:47.390
and concentrate on his
research so that there

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:49.490
is not a repeat of what just happened.

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:52.630
What?! Th-that’s absurd!

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:54.530
I-I could never step down--

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:55.780
Very well.

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:57.910
S-Serizawa-sensei!

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:02.910
V-very well.

00:10:03.550 --> 00:10:05.800
Then Niimi-san and Kodo-san will

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:07.800
conduct experiments on the medicine.

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:10.780
I shall offer you my assistance.

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:15.050
Everyone is dismissed for tonight.

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:17.890
Do not tell others about this.

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:19.250
Got that?

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:24.240
Is that a letter from Toku-san in Edo?

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:25.680
Yeah.

00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:30.070
As always, she says
to take care of myself

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:32.230
and not to go losing my temper

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:34.420
and picking fights with our soldiers.

00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:35.940
It’s the same as always.

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:41.260
My big sis is still treating
me like a little kid!

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:43.740
She’s worried about you.

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:47.200
I wish she’d have a
bit more faith in me...

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:55.330
What is the matter?

00:10:57.010 --> 00:10:59.170
How am I supposed to respond?

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:02.300
Even though I got to stay in Kyoto,

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:05.350
Serizawa-san has been carrying
us through everything.

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:06.560
Toshi-san?

00:11:07.670 --> 00:11:12.100
In the end, I haven’t accomplished
a damn thing on my own.

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:14.340
To top it off,

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:17.360
now we’re stuck relying
on some eerie medicine.

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:19.880
We’re even sacrificing men...

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:22.990
That isn’t your fault, Toshi-san!

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:24.940
At this rate,

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:27.280
the Roshigumi is going to
turn into some shady organization.

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:29.480
We’re going down a direction that

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:31.340
differs from what we were aiming for.

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:34.750
We can’t keep on as we have.

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:39.030
I still lack resolve...

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:43.760
I’m not one to chastise Ibuki, am I?

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:46.760
Toshi-san...

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:49.640
There is no need for you
to bear this on your own.

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:51.770
Gen-san...

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:54.520
We will help you bear
these heavy burdens.

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:57.630
We will accompany you
no matter where you go.

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:00.860
Thanks.

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:04.470
Bluntly put, the Shogunate and

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:05.920
the Aizu Domain want to

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:08.290
use us to do their dirty work, right?

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:12.000
That is the extent of
our worth at present.

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:14.380
Sannan-san, are you okay with this?!

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:17.670
Can you keep your cool if one of your

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:19.740
buddies get turned into a monster?!

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:21.580
Do you think I am okay with this?

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:34.440
Damn it!

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:42.860
Oh, Ibuki-kun! I’d like
you to join us in the hall.

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:46.390
Can’t. Niimi-san sent me over to drop

00:12:46.390 --> 00:12:47.870
this off with Sannan-san.

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:49.450
Then this works out well!

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:52.160
Sannan-kun and the others
are all waiting in the hall.

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:55.710
We’re greeting the new recruits.

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:01.740
Long time no see, Nagakura-san.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:06.390
Oh, it’s you!

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:08.460
What is it, Shinpachi?

00:13:08.460 --> 00:13:09.720
You know him?

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:12.070
Yeah. Back in Edo

00:13:12.070 --> 00:13:15.140
we attended the
Shingyoto-style dojo together.

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:17.800
My name is Kai Shimada.

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:21.530
I was studying the spear at a dojo

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:23.530
in Osaka until just the other day.

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:23.530
What’re you doing here?

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:25.420
Beats me!

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:27.570
I heard that the Roshigumi
was recruiting, so...

00:13:25.420 --> 00:13:27.940
Kondou-san said I should
make their acquaintance

00:13:27.940 --> 00:13:30.110
since we’ll be living in
the headquarters together.

00:13:27.940 --> 00:13:30.110
We’ll be a hundred men
stronger with you by our side!

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:31.660
It’s a pleasure being here!

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:34.910
Okay, next!

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:37.040
I am Susumu Yamazaki.

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:39.170
It is a pleasure to
make your acquaintance.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:42.200
Weren’t you born in Osaka?

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:45.170
Sir! My father was an acupuncturist.

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:48.470
So do you possess medical knowledge?

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:49.680
A little.

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:51.120
Great!

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:55.150
We may need to make use
of that knowledge someday.

00:13:55.150 --> 00:13:56.190
Sir!

00:13:56.190 --> 00:13:57.730
Okay, next!

00:13:57.730 --> 00:14:00.230
Sir! I am Katsuji Kawashima.

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:01.650
It is a pleasure to meet you!

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:04.560
This is everyone, right?

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:07.890
Once you join the Roshigumi,

00:14:07.890 --> 00:14:10.630
regardless of your birth and rearing

00:14:10.630 --> 00:14:12.270
we will treat your like warriors.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:14.910
Are you ready for this?

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:16.210
Sir!

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:18.860
From here out, let’s combine our forces

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:20.810
By the way, why isn’t
Serizawa-san here?

00:14:18.860 --> 00:14:21.190
to crackdown on the rogue samurai

00:14:21.190 --> 00:14:23.170
who are disturbing the peace in Kyoto.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:25.460
Apparently he said he would leave
everything to Chief Kondou.

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:27.110
Guys, I want you to maintain
an indomitable resolve.

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:28.170
No matter who joins,

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:30.720
it doesn’t matter to that man.

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:32.260
I’m counting on you!

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:33.600
Sir!

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:40.270
It is well known that the
rogue samurai’s main base

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:42.620
has moved from Kyoto to Osaka since the

00:14:42.620 --> 00:14:46.360
Kyoto Military Commissioner
was put into office last year.

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:50.110
As such, rather than pursue essentially

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:52.460
fruitless patrols in Kyoto,

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:57.630
couldn’t we earn merits
faster by visiting Osaka

00:14:57.630 --> 00:15:00.000
and arresting some ronin?

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:01.540
Fruitless patro--

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:03.130
You may be right.

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:07.000
Let’s prepare to leave
for Osaka right away.

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:11.020
I will let you decide who is coming.

00:15:11.020 --> 00:15:12.010
Very well.

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:15.510
Make sure to select men who can kill.

00:15:17.610 --> 00:15:18.340
Okay...

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:22.970
Dog, you’re coming as well.

00:15:22.970 --> 00:15:23.770
Huh?

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:28.340
But I don’t think I’d
be of much help if I went.

00:15:28.340 --> 00:15:30.250
If you don’t come,

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:33.430
who will carry my luggage?

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:37.040
The least you could do
is carry your own crap!

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:39.040
What was that?!

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:42.580
Master, I shall accompany you!

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:45.930
I have some work I would like
Ibuki-san to attend to here.

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:48.170
Humph!

00:15:48.790 --> 00:15:50.070
Do as you wish.

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:05.060
What was it you wanted
me to take care of?

00:16:05.060 --> 00:16:07.310
Oh, that was a lie.

00:16:07.310 --> 00:16:08.570
A lie?

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:10.500
If I didn’t say that,

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:13.570
the master would
have forced you to go with him.

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:16.590
So you’re sacrificing
yourself for me...?

00:16:16.590 --> 00:16:19.190
It’s nothing that grand!

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:25.420
Please relax and spread your
wings while we’re in Osaka.

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:28.690
Hirama-san, thank you.

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:32.840
Serizawa-sama and the others
are departing for Osaka?

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:36.850
Yukimura-dono!

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:39.560
I’ve been eagerly
awaiting your arrival!

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:42.640
I could use your advice
on something today.

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:43.510
Okay.

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:46.210
Come, come. Please, come inside!

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:48.030
It’s freaky how happy Niimi-san is.

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:50.810
That’s because Sannan-san,
who’d always

00:16:50.810 --> 00:16:53.020
voice his opposition, left for Osaka.

00:16:53.020 --> 00:16:53.820
Heisuke!

00:16:57.490 --> 00:17:00.400
Please keep an eye on
Niimi-san and Kodo-san.

00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:01.250
What?

00:17:01.690 --> 00:17:05.070
Niimi-san intends to get the jump
on us

00:17:05.070 --> 00:17:06.710
while Sannan-san is away

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:10.460
and proceed with the
experiments with Kodo-san.

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:12.380
No kidding.

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:15.290
I can’t leave Kyoto,

00:17:15.290 --> 00:17:17.990
so I had Sannan-san go to Osaka.

00:17:17.990 --> 00:17:20.510
But I don’t intend to let
them do as they please.

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:24.010
So you had me stay rather
than go to Osaka because...

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:26.270
I can only entrust this job

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:28.520
with someone who knows about

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:32.260
the Water of Life and furies and is
also a trustworthy companion.

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:33.340
Got it!

00:17:33.340 --> 00:17:36.530
So it wasn’t because you
lacked faith in my abilities!

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:38.120
Of course not!

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:39.830
So that means you don’t

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:43.240
want to rely on that
medicine either, right?

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:44.540
You’re being too loud.

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:45.660
Oh, sorry.

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:49.120
Harada and I are going to the
magistrate’s office now.

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:50.670
I’m counting on you.

00:17:51.720 --> 00:17:53.200
Leave them to me!

00:17:57.260 --> 00:17:58.930
I am leaving now.

00:17:58.930 --> 00:17:59.820
Okay.

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:07.560
I’ll walk you home.

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:11.690
It’d suck if you got attacked by
rogue samurai on your way back.

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:15.580
No, I will be fine.

00:18:15.580 --> 00:18:17.950
I appreciate your concern.

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:20.070
Is your research progressing any?

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:25.790
This is not something that will
produce results overnight.

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:33.070
It would appear you think poorly of our

00:18:33.070 --> 00:18:36.800
conducting research on the Water of Life.

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:40.140
Yeah. I understand our situation.

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:42.120
But even so,

00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:44.720
I don’t want my
friends to take that medicine.

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:47.770
Indeed, it is not
something we should use.

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:54.980
However, it is also a fact that
countless lives will be saved

00:18:54.980 --> 00:18:57.360
by that medicine’s powers.

00:18:57.610 --> 00:18:59.330
Save lives?

00:18:59.330 --> 00:19:01.460
With a medicine that
turns people into monsters?

00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:07.330
Any who lose everything due to
their own powerlessness think,

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:11.130
“If only I had more power.”

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:16.980
The power obtained through
the Water of Life is fake.

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:20.730
It may not be true power,

00:19:20.730 --> 00:19:23.680
yet even if it is fake,

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:25.760
there are things you can protect

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:28.770
so long as you possess it.

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:32.270
Do you have a reason for
seeking greater power?

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:36.650
I cannot say. I am simply a doctor.

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:41.410
If the power you seek brings us harm,

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:46.740
I will kill you on the spot!

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:52.830
Everyone has their own position,
ideas and ambitions!

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:55.040
It’s nice when you can talk things out,

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:56.910
but when you can’t...

00:19:56.910 --> 00:20:01.550
When two adamant wills clash,
fighting is the only option.

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:03.760
That’s what I think.

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:07.230
Even so, if possible...

00:20:07.230 --> 00:20:10.390
I don’t want
to kill someone if I don’t have to.

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:13.600
I think it’d be great if
I never had to kill anyone.

00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:17.140
Farewell.

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:28.270
If you lack the resolve to kill

00:20:28.270 --> 00:20:31.210
someone when you draw
that, get out of here!

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:33.720
If you lack any real resolve,

00:20:33.720 --> 00:20:36.470
don’t waltz out onto a battlefield.

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:41.290
What do I have...?

00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:47.450
Several Days Later

00:20:45.050 --> 00:20:46.360
Serizawa-san!

00:20:46.360 --> 00:20:47.470
A moment please!

00:20:47.810 --> 00:20:49.040
Quit harping!

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:54.480
Move it, cur!

00:20:55.310 --> 00:20:56.690
Ow!

00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:07.370
Welcome back, Kondou-san.

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:15.040
Shinpatsu, did you have any luck?

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:24.760
Sannan-san, did something happen?

00:21:25.970 --> 00:21:28.660
There was a scuffle with some

00:21:28.660 --> 00:21:30.740
unarmed sumo wrestlers in Osaka...

00:21:31.170 --> 00:21:32.640
A scuffle?

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:38.150
Serizawa-san and Okita-kun...

00:21:47.820 --> 00:21:50.010
...struck down the wrestlers.

00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:51.800
They what?!

00:23:28.010 --> 00:23:30.880
Why, exactly, are you here?

00:23:31.180 --> 00:23:32.380
I’m here to make Kondou-san

00:23:32.380 --> 00:23:34.440
the head warrior in the
fight for a just cause.

00:23:34.440 --> 00:23:38.390
Hijikata, you must become a devil!

00:23:39.390 --> 00:23:41.400
Oath Made on the Wind
Blowing Over the Grass
